.fi
.RE
.SS iq config view
Print the whole config as TOML, URLs redacted
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR iq config view
.PP
\fBFlags:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-expand\fR
resolve keyring\-backed passwords and inline them into printed URLs
.TP
\fB\-\-reveal\fR
print inline\-stored passwords verbatim instead of redacting them
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.RS
.nf
  $ iq config view
.fi
.RE
.SS iq driver
Inspect the backends iq can talk to
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR iq driver
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.RS
.nf
  $ iq driver ls # list the backend drivers iq can dispatch to
.fi
.RE
.SS iq driver ls
List the backend drivers iq can dispatch to
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR iq driver ls
.PP
List the backend drivers iq can dispatch to. Each row shows the driver's stable name (as `iq ls` reports it), a description, the URL schemes that select it, the backend server versions the bundled client library supports, and a link to its upstream documentation. \-v appends the file driver's readable dump formats (which auto\-detect, which need ?format=). \-j/\-\-json or \-y/\-\-yaml emit machine\-readable output.
.PP
\fBFlags:\fR
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
emit machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yaml\fR
emit machine\-readable YAML
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.RS
.nf
  $ iq driver ls    # list the backend drivers
  $ iq driver ls \-v # also list the file driver's dump formats
.fi
.RE
